    "body": "progress: bherbruck · 2026-11-07T22:58:33Z · fix committed on issue/122-face-from-stock (fork bherbruck/Camcraft): `turning::facing` takes the setup's stock beside the part (axis still fitted to the part), so the ladder climbs to the stock's end. Pinned by `turning_face::a_stock_allowance_above_the_finished_part_is_faced_off`, `drill_prior::a_stock_facing_allowance_is_faced_and_the_drill_after_it_stands` and `::a_finished_part_with_no_stock_allowance_has_nothing_to_face` (pass). Note: posting the whole face-then-drill lathe program is still refused by the footprint rapid law on Op1's inward rapids - that's #159 (same refusal on main, rides #135), so the pin asserts facing + drill verdicts and can gain the post line after #159. Turning/lathe gate running; PR follows when green.",
